WEBVTT

00:06.520 --> 00:07.520
[Tommy] Arthur.

00:09.680 --> 00:10.680
John.

00:13.600 --> 00:14.600
Michael.

00:17.200 --> 00:21.200
The chief constable of Birmingham
has issued a warrant for your arrest.

00:26.760 --> 00:29.320
[indistinct chatter]

00:30.040 --> 00:33.800
I've made a deal with people
even more powerful than our enemies.

00:38.400 --> 00:39.400
Trust me, brother.

00:48.400 --> 00:49.400
[bell tolling at a distance]

01:01.480 --> 01:02.480
[Arthur] Father.

01:03.440 --> 01:04.800
What is it, Sunday?

01:05.160 --> 01:06.160
[Michael] There's been a mistake.

01:07.120 --> 01:09.720
There's an appeal process underway
that doesn't begin until January.

01:09.800 --> 01:11.840
I want to see my lawyer, Mr. Patrick.

01:11.920 --> 01:12.920
Stop!

01:13.520 --> 01:14.560
This shouldn't be happening.

01:14.640 --> 01:15.640
[John screaming]

01:21.320 --> 01:22.720
[John] Get your hands off me!

01:32.680 --> 01:35.600
Move out! I'm John Shelby.

01:43.200 --> 01:45.760
[Polly] ...clean up when I come back.
When I come back I gotta be clean.

01:46.200 --> 01:48.560
Whatever I said, whatever I decided.

01:48.840 --> 01:50.200
Whatever I decide...

02:12.840 --> 02:14.880
[Arthur] Michael? Michael?

02:14.960 --> 02:15.960
[Michael] Arthur!

02:16.520 --> 02:18.320
-[Michael] Arthur!
-John!

02:18.400 --> 02:19.400
Where's Tommy?

02:19.480 --> 02:22.000
-Arthur! Arthur!
-No!

02:30.320 --> 02:31.720
[Polly gasping]

02:32.680 --> 02:33.680
No.

02:52.880 --> 02:54.320
[barrister] Arthur,
you have to call the King.

02:55.800 --> 02:57.840
-About what?
-About this.

02:59.080 --> 03:01.200
This is the case of a family
of Birmingham gangsters

03:01.280 --> 03:03.160
on trial for murder and sedition.

03:04.000 --> 03:05.040
Why would the King intervene?

03:05.480 --> 03:07.600
The leader of the gang, Thomas Shelby,

03:08.000 --> 03:10.640
he claims his family was
caught up in a wider conspiracy.

03:10.880 --> 03:12.160
He names Winston Churchill.

03:12.280 --> 03:13.320
You woke me up for this?

03:13.480 --> 03:15.320
And he also sent us this.

03:18.720 --> 03:21.280
[judge]
How the fuck did a Birmingham racketeer

03:21.360 --> 03:25.640
get his hands on a personal letter
written by King George?

03:26.080 --> 03:27.600
[barrister] During a robbery
at Hampton Court,

03:27.680 --> 03:29.840
Shelby discovered a box of correspondence.

03:30.160 --> 03:32.600
Among the papers he stole
was that letter from the King himself,

03:33.400 --> 03:35.560
which proves his Majesty was involved.

03:36.640 --> 03:38.200
Uh, utter fuck.

03:40.520 --> 03:41.640
[barrister] If his family walks free

03:41.720 --> 03:44.000
then he will burn the papers
in my presence.

03:45.360 --> 03:46.640
[judge] When are they due to hang?

03:47.440 --> 03:50.360
Today. This morning
in Winston Green prison.

03:51.080 --> 03:52.800
Why the hell
didn't you bring it up before?

03:53.480 --> 03:55.000
[barrister] The plan was
for the Lord Chamberlain

03:55.080 --> 03:56.520
to intervene at the appeal

03:56.640 --> 03:59.680
but late last night some local judge
brought the executions forward.

03:59.760 --> 04:01.000
Oh, my giddy heart.

04:02.960 --> 04:04.680
Put me through to his Majesty.

04:05.920 --> 04:07.240
Well, wake him up!

04:19.440 --> 04:21.880
In the bleak midwinter.

04:23.240 --> 04:24.600
In the bleak midwinter.

04:24.960 --> 04:27.120
Thy Kingdom come. Thy will be done...

04:28.560 --> 04:29.680
[Polly] Help, Lord Jesus,

04:30.280 --> 04:33.040
with this rope pull me up to heaven.

04:34.160 --> 04:37.800
I see your face shining down on me.

04:53.760 --> 04:55.000
[warden] Wait!

04:59.880 --> 05:02.360
Wait!

05:19.120 --> 05:22.360
Also, sir, in return
for burning the King's letters

05:22.520 --> 05:24.040
Thomas Shelby has asked
for something else,

05:25.080 --> 05:27.200
inclusion in this year's
New Year's Honors List.

05:28.240 --> 05:31.200
Thomas Shelby has asked for the King
to award him an OBE, sir.

05:50.800 --> 05:54.400
♪ Take a little walk
To the edge of town ♪

05:54.480 --> 05:56.680
♪ And go across the tracks ♪

05:57.000 --> 05:58.640
Oh, God bless. Merry Christmas.

05:58.880 --> 06:00.800
♪ Where the viaduct looms ♪

06:00.960 --> 06:02.800
♪ Like a bird of doom ♪

06:03.080 --> 06:06.080
♪ As it shifts and cracks ♪

06:07.160 --> 06:11.120
♪ Where secrets lie
In the border fires ♪

06:11.240 --> 06:13.280
♪ In the humming wires ♪

06:13.360 --> 06:14.360
♪ Hey man, you know ♪

06:14.480 --> 06:16.200
♪ You're never coming back ♪

06:16.320 --> 06:18.360
♪ Past the square
Past the bridge ♪

06:18.480 --> 06:21.200
♪ Past the mills
Past the stacks ♪

06:23.560 --> 06:26.040
♪ On a gathering storm comes ♪

06:26.120 --> 06:27.880
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

06:28.000 --> 06:29.720
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

06:29.840 --> 06:32.360
♪ A red right hand ♪

06:42.280 --> 06:44.240
Not going home for Christmas, Mr. Shelby?

06:45.280 --> 06:46.280
Tomorrow.

06:46.920 --> 06:50.040
So, Maria or Clara?

06:50.720 --> 06:51.800
Or Elizabeth?

06:53.680 --> 06:54.680
It's Christmas,

06:55.480 --> 06:56.560
someone new, Billy.

07:03.320 --> 07:05.600
I've wrapped all Charlie's presents
and left them in the room.

07:07.280 --> 07:08.280
What did I get him?

07:08.800 --> 07:11.880
Toy horses, toy cars, toy guns.

07:13.640 --> 07:16.000
You're due at the Singer factory
at 8:00 tomorrow, not 8:30,

07:16.080 --> 07:17.080
there's a union problem.

07:18.160 --> 07:19.160
Eight, yep.

07:19.960 --> 07:21.320
And the driver will take you home.

07:22.240 --> 07:23.440
I'll drive meself.

07:23.840 --> 07:25.520
Goodnight Lizzie, have a good Christmas.

07:28.240 --> 07:30.120
-I'll have a vodka tonic.
-Yes, ma'am.

07:38.520 --> 07:42.400
Tommy, I've had Christmas cards
from John, Arthur, Ada, Michael and Polly.

07:46.920 --> 07:48.120
And an invitation,

07:49.320 --> 07:50.320
New Year's.

07:50.840 --> 07:52.240
Party at John's house.

07:52.680 --> 07:55.120
A party at John's big house, good for him.

07:56.440 --> 07:58.360
Ada's coming back from Boston for it.

07:58.720 --> 07:59.720
I know.

08:00.560 --> 08:02.480
It was me who gave her the time off.

08:07.160 --> 08:10.600
Why don't you come?
Just turn up, bring Charlie,

08:11.040 --> 08:13.080
bring a lump of coal, first footing.

08:14.240 --> 08:17.360
Dark-haired man crosses the threshold
to bring good luck for the new year.

08:17.840 --> 08:18.840
Mmm?

08:19.120 --> 08:22.160
The babies will make everybody okay,
babies stop everything.

08:22.840 --> 08:25.320
Can't pull a razor with a baby there,
not even Esme.

08:30.840 --> 08:31.840
Just come.

08:32.720 --> 08:33.880
See what happens.

08:38.000 --> 08:42.080
Tommy, you've never even seen
Arthur's kid, nor John and Esme's.

08:43.679 --> 08:44.680
Your drink, madam.

08:45.080 --> 08:46.080
Thank you.

08:46.600 --> 08:47.600
Billy,

08:49.480 --> 08:50.480
who did you get for me?

08:55.440 --> 08:57.440
-Theresa.
-I said someone new.

08:58.200 --> 08:59.200
Understood.

09:04.400 --> 09:05.800
Do it for Charlie.

09:06.560 --> 09:08.280
Charlie should know his cousins.

09:10.880 --> 09:13.560
I'll get Charlie a real horse, Lizzie,

09:15.080 --> 09:17.280
not a toy, a thoroughbred.

09:18.840 --> 09:20.680
And on Christmas day
it'll be just you and Charlie.

09:22.440 --> 09:23.440
And the horse.

09:28.120 --> 09:29.920
Can't live like this another year.

09:33.440 --> 09:36.360
Sex, freedom, whiskey sours,

09:38.120 --> 09:40.640
which one should I give up first,
Lizzie, eh?

09:49.480 --> 09:50.480
I got you something.

10:02.600 --> 10:03.800
Merry Christmas.

10:58.840 --> 11:01.120
I told you you didn't need to come
on Christmas Eve,

11:01.400 --> 11:02.520
I could've dealt with it.

11:02.600 --> 11:04.520
Yeah, like you dealt with it

11:04.840 --> 11:06.280
at the pressings factory.

11:06.800 --> 11:08.120
Well, this is the same problem.

11:09.480 --> 11:11.360
Same fucking union convenor.

11:12.120 --> 11:14.840
Area convenor for the boiler makers union
has got involved with something

11:14.920 --> 11:17.840
that could've otherwise been fixed
with a drink and a bribe.

11:18.600 --> 11:20.160
-A wire cutting shop?
-Hmm,

11:20.600 --> 11:22.160
and all the wire cutters here are women,

11:22.240 --> 11:24.640
that's why the union convenor thinks
they're being underpaid.

11:26.680 --> 11:27.680
Well, tell him

11:28.080 --> 11:31.000
there are no men in the cutting shop
so there can be no comparatives.

11:31.480 --> 11:32.480
It's a woman.

11:32.760 --> 11:33.760
What is?

11:34.120 --> 11:35.680
The union convenor
causing all the trouble.

11:37.720 --> 11:38.720
Fuck her.

11:38.960 --> 11:40.440
Her name's Jessie Eden.

11:42.360 --> 11:43.680
-You heard of her?
-Yeah.

11:44.880 --> 11:45.880
Do you want me in the meeting?

11:47.280 --> 11:48.280
No.

11:51.840 --> 11:52.840
Michael?

12:10.200 --> 12:11.200
Look,

12:12.360 --> 12:14.720
sometimes I have a sniff of snow, so what?

12:15.040 --> 12:16.040
How's your mother?

12:18.280 --> 12:21.160
I drove past her house,
the drain pipe was hanging off.

12:23.680 --> 12:25.440
Look, the cocaine keeps me awake.

12:26.960 --> 12:29.120
Very long hours these days
and when I do sleep

12:29.200 --> 12:30.320
I dream about what happened.

12:31.480 --> 12:33.840
I wasn't asking about you, Michael, was I?

12:35.880 --> 12:37.240
I was asking about your mother.

12:39.640 --> 12:41.960
Since she was pardoned,
she's been on these fucking tablets

12:42.040 --> 12:43.760
the doctor gave her
when she was in the prison.

12:44.520 --> 12:46.600
She says that
when she was inside the noose

12:47.560 --> 12:48.800
she saw spirits.

12:50.440 --> 12:51.760
She's running séances

12:52.120 --> 12:54.080
but people just come into the house
to steal things.

12:56.280 --> 12:58.800
-Tommy, it's bad.
-All right, all right.

13:01.600 --> 13:02.600
[clears throat]

13:02.720 --> 13:03.840
All right, listen to me, Michael,

13:09.800 --> 13:11.280
the spirits she sees...

13:12.040 --> 13:13.040
are real.

13:14.360 --> 13:15.560
Believe they're real.

13:16.520 --> 13:17.680
Believe it with her.

13:18.400 --> 13:19.400
And eventually,

13:20.400 --> 13:21.960
you can take the remembered noose

13:22.520 --> 13:23.640
from around her neck,

13:24.680 --> 13:25.760
like a horse

13:26.160 --> 13:27.160
that's been choked off.

13:28.920 --> 13:30.000
Keep her off whiskey,

13:30.680 --> 13:31.920
throw away the tablets,

13:33.360 --> 13:35.000
and stop giving her fucking snow.

13:37.640 --> 13:38.640
Fuck, Tommy,

13:39.080 --> 13:40.760
sounds like family advice.

13:42.440 --> 13:43.440
You coming back?

13:45.600 --> 13:46.800
Nothing to come back to.

13:50.040 --> 13:51.480
Truth is they're all fucked.

13:52.560 --> 13:53.560
The lot of them.

13:54.560 --> 13:55.560
Yeah.

13:59.960 --> 14:01.640
Find out about that woman, Jessie Eden.

14:02.680 --> 14:05.280
Don't let your mother
keep cash in the house. And oi,

14:06.720 --> 14:09.000
no cocaine on the registered premises.

15:03.040 --> 15:04.480
Did you see they all came?

15:07.280 --> 15:08.720
Yeah, I saw you at the back.

15:11.720 --> 15:13.200
It's funny they don't notice.

15:18.320 --> 15:19.600
Oh, my sweet.

15:21.120 --> 15:22.280
Oh, my heart.

15:26.200 --> 15:28.080
Crushed to death in the canal...

15:29.920 --> 15:31.360
but back home again.

15:32.240 --> 15:35.080
It's so beautiful.

15:43.440 --> 15:44.440
[sighs]

15:51.800 --> 15:52.920
Inside the loop.

15:58.960 --> 16:00.840
Inside the merry loop.

16:04.200 --> 16:05.600
[footsteps approaching]

16:32.840 --> 16:34.080
For fuck's sake.

16:42.560 --> 16:43.760
Fucking birds.

16:50.320 --> 16:51.320
Ada.

16:53.760 --> 16:54.760
Come on.

17:04.960 --> 17:06.880
Thought we lost you
to the Great White Way of Broadway.

17:07.359 --> 17:08.359
No.

17:08.680 --> 17:10.560
Well, this beats Watery Lane, John.

17:10.680 --> 17:11.680
Does it?

17:11.839 --> 17:13.520
Here, take a seat, I'll grab the kids.

17:14.160 --> 17:15.160
No, it's all right,

17:16.160 --> 17:17.160
I'm not stopping.

17:17.480 --> 17:19.800
Just wanna drop those presents off
for tomorrow.

17:20.040 --> 17:21.680
I don't want words on Christmas Eve.

17:21.880 --> 17:23.040
Well, it's my house, you're welcome.

17:25.640 --> 17:27.079
It's okay, I'm staying with Polly.

17:27.960 --> 17:30.480
Huh, she's in a bad way.

17:31.840 --> 17:33.560
I'll bring her to her senses.

17:33.920 --> 17:35.200
Michael's already tried that.

17:35.400 --> 17:36.480
I'll get through to her.

17:39.800 --> 17:41.920
You still gonna come to the party
on New Year's Eve?

17:42.040 --> 17:43.400
Yeah, who else is coming?

17:43.880 --> 17:45.680
Arthur, Linda.

17:47.320 --> 17:48.320
Hello, Esme.

17:51.320 --> 17:53.080
Who paid for your car and driver, Ada?

17:54.080 --> 17:55.600
Shelby Company Limited.

17:56.720 --> 17:58.960
Nice car, treats you well,

17:59.360 --> 18:00.560
his last little pet.

18:01.920 --> 18:04.760
Look, this visit is meant to be
about making things all right.

18:05.880 --> 18:07.800
John had a rope around his neck,
he shit himself.

18:07.880 --> 18:09.720
All right, Esme, that'll do, yeah.

18:10.240 --> 18:11.360
Go on, go in the kitchen.

18:12.360 --> 18:14.480
Take the cars back to the money.

18:21.480 --> 18:23.040
Anyway, there's your presents.

18:24.200 --> 18:25.200
How's Arthur?

18:26.560 --> 18:28.680
Uh, for Christmas get him a sewing kit,

18:29.640 --> 18:31.720
so he can sew his fucking balls back on.

19:02.640 --> 19:03.880
[telephone ringing]

19:12.480 --> 19:13.760
Maypole 245.

19:17.320 --> 19:18.320
Hello, Esme.

19:18.920 --> 19:22.040
There you go, look, couple of eggs, eh,
it's two eggs.

19:23.160 --> 19:24.160
Off you go.

19:24.760 --> 19:25.760
Arthur,

19:25.920 --> 19:28.000
be careful with Billy in there,
there's a cock.

19:28.160 --> 19:29.160
Yeah, I will.

19:30.000 --> 19:31.560
And don't smoke that near him.

19:32.240 --> 19:33.240
All right.

19:34.000 --> 19:35.000
Get out of it.

19:35.080 --> 19:37.280
Esme called to say Ada's on her way over.

19:39.400 --> 19:40.960
Did you hear that, Billy boy?

19:41.360 --> 19:44.600
Your aunty Ada's coming,
all the way from America.

19:46.480 --> 19:47.480
Bye, chicken.

19:48.360 --> 19:50.120
Oh, I dropped an egg, look.

19:50.920 --> 19:52.600
I dropped an egg, Billy boy.

20:01.000 --> 20:03.120
Give him the hell he gives us, Ms. Eden.

20:27.680 --> 20:30.200
Excuse me. This is the gents' lav.

20:30.280 --> 20:32.360
You don't have a women's lavatory
on the second floor,

20:32.440 --> 20:34.160
because no women get this far up.

20:34.800 --> 20:38.520
If you don't have a women's lavatory
I can't go to it, can I?

20:59.000 --> 21:01.920
You say there is a disparity in pay
based on sex.

21:06.080 --> 21:08.000
The male wire cutters
in the Rover factory,

21:08.080 --> 21:09.600
a mile and a half down the road

21:09.800 --> 21:13.920
are paid ten shillings a week more
than the female wire cutters here.

21:14.760 --> 21:16.480
Different factories, different rates.

21:16.920 --> 21:19.280
But both factories
are owned by you, Mr. Shelby.

21:19.920 --> 21:21.440
Not in your own name, of course,

21:21.880 --> 21:23.720
in the name of other house holdings.

21:24.640 --> 21:28.320
You own the Manchester Car and Van Factory
in the name of Tilting Company Limited,

21:28.640 --> 21:30.840
the Billings Machine
tools factories at Hay Mills

21:30.920 --> 21:33.040
in Greet in the name of
Stechford Engineering.

21:33.200 --> 21:36.280
The Bilstone Forgings and Presses Factory
in the name of Canalside

21:36.360 --> 21:38.400
and the Canal Warehousing in Gas Street.

21:38.520 --> 21:41.240
Sortley in Cadbury in the name of
Shelby Company Limited,

21:41.320 --> 21:45.320
also 255 streets of back to back houses.

21:47.200 --> 21:48.200
Very good.

21:49.800 --> 21:50.800
Very good.

21:52.120 --> 21:53.240
So this isn't about

21:53.840 --> 21:56.560
women and men, it's about me, eh?

21:57.480 --> 22:01.200
Tommy Shelby, OBE, no it's not about you.

22:02.360 --> 22:03.640
It's about disparities.

22:04.520 --> 22:06.280
It's about ten shillings a week
for working mothers

22:06.360 --> 22:07.760
so they can buy shoes for their kids.

22:07.840 --> 22:10.280
-Never had shoes meself.
-So now you deny others?

22:11.400 --> 22:13.200
And barefoot I grew up mean.

22:13.560 --> 22:14.560
Oh, I know.

22:14.640 --> 22:15.920
Oh, yeah, you know everything.

22:16.160 --> 22:18.160
-Your turn of phrase--
-Is unacceptable?

22:18.240 --> 22:20.560
You grew up mean you say,
threat in there I think somewhere.

22:20.640 --> 22:21.640
No threats.

22:21.720 --> 22:23.680
The whole of Birmingham
knows you, Mr. Shelby.

22:23.760 --> 22:24.760
Sweetheart,

22:25.920 --> 22:26.920
whatever you've heard,

22:27.840 --> 22:29.360
I don't need to make threats.

22:32.800 --> 22:34.320
My comrade brothers and sisters--

22:34.560 --> 22:36.560
Your brothers and sisters,
all right, listen,

22:37.400 --> 22:39.720
I will conduct myself as a businessman.

22:39.880 --> 22:40.920
Who says sweetheart.

22:41.000 --> 22:44.840
You say there's a ten shilling disparity
between male and female cutters

22:44.960 --> 22:47.200
in two of my factories. Very well,

22:48.800 --> 22:51.160
I will increase the pay
of the female cutters

22:51.240 --> 22:53.240
in this factory by five shillings

22:54.440 --> 22:57.000
and I will cut the pay of the male cutters

22:57.160 --> 22:59.480
in the Rover by five shillings,

23:00.560 --> 23:03.240
thereby achieving
your sacred fucking parity.

23:04.760 --> 23:05.920
And I will tell the men

23:06.440 --> 23:07.840
with families to feed

23:08.640 --> 23:10.600
whose idea it was to cut their pay.

23:11.040 --> 23:14.600
You do that, I will bring
all my members out on strike.

23:14.680 --> 23:15.680
Oh, yeah?

23:15.840 --> 23:17.480
A week after Christmas, do you think so?

23:18.080 --> 23:19.480
You know, everything
you've said here today

23:19.560 --> 23:21.360
and the fact that
we're having this meeting today

23:22.160 --> 23:24.920
tells me that you're a woman
without a family.

23:26.320 --> 23:30.200
And everything I hear about you tells me
you're a man without a family as well.

23:32.120 --> 23:35.240
My comrade brothers and sisters
are not afraid of you, Mr. Shelby.

23:35.880 --> 23:38.760
I will call an extraordinary meeting
of my executive committee

23:38.840 --> 23:40.000
as soon as Boxing Day.

23:40.520 --> 23:42.680
You will hear the whistles blow
all across Birmingham.

23:45.720 --> 23:48.000
I've heard
lots of whistles blow, sweetheart.

24:13.320 --> 24:15.080
The post has arrived, Mr. Shelby.

24:22.960 --> 24:23.960
I'm sorry to keep asking

24:24.040 --> 24:26.320
but Chef needs to know
how many for dinner tomorrow.

24:27.520 --> 24:28.520
He's new,

24:28.800 --> 24:30.680
he's foreign, he gets very upset.

24:32.960 --> 24:34.160
Oh, will you tell Chef

24:34.240 --> 24:36.840
there'll be 27 guests
for Christmas dinner tomorrow.

24:36.920 --> 24:37.920
27?

24:38.400 --> 24:39.600
-Family?
-Yep.

24:40.320 --> 24:42.200
I thought Charlie could do
with some company

24:42.280 --> 24:45.280
so I asked Johnny Dogs
if he knew anyone who liked to eat goose

24:46.360 --> 24:48.080
and he said he knew 26.

24:50.360 --> 24:54.240
Tell Chef I want ten geese,
a buck cut into steaks,

24:55.200 --> 24:56.680
some trout from the river,

24:58.000 --> 25:00.680
fetch whiskey, brandy and wine
from the cellar, best we have.

25:01.760 --> 25:02.960
There will be children?

25:03.680 --> 25:04.760
Lots of children.

25:05.280 --> 25:07.960
With Johnny's tribe, new ones
might be born on the floor,

25:08.560 --> 25:11.520
so have, have mops and buckets ready, eh?

25:12.920 --> 25:15.680
And I want you at the table, Frances,
so make it 28.

25:16.680 --> 25:18.000
I will be busy.

25:19.320 --> 25:20.600
You've put up with me this past year,

25:20.680 --> 25:22.480
looked after Charlie
when I've been on business.

25:22.560 --> 25:25.240
Tomorrow, you will eat at my table.

25:28.440 --> 25:30.280
Things will get better I think next year.

25:34.240 --> 25:35.240
Uh-huh.

25:42.080 --> 25:43.080
[door closes]

26:33.040 --> 26:34.920
[Ada] Gets much warmer than here
in the summer,

26:35.480 --> 26:37.320
-much colder in the winter.
-[Arthur] I knew it.

26:38.000 --> 26:39.600
But parts of it are just like Birmingham.

26:39.920 --> 26:42.880
Yeah. Shit and smoke the same everywhere.

26:43.840 --> 26:45.120
[Ada] What about you, Linda?

26:45.640 --> 26:46.640
You working?

26:47.760 --> 26:49.280
I've been seeking work as a teacher.

26:49.600 --> 26:51.360
-[Arthur] Teacher.
-Hmm, but you know,

26:51.680 --> 26:54.920
it's quite difficult. The Shelby name
is always in the papers.

26:56.880 --> 26:59.120
And, uh, what do you get up to
all day, Arthur?

26:59.920 --> 27:03.320
As you know Arthur's previous endeavors
have left us with no need for a salary.

27:04.720 --> 27:06.720
Arthur occupies his time in the garden,

27:07.080 --> 27:08.640
doing voluntary work.

27:09.360 --> 27:11.000
He drives old people and cripples.

27:11.680 --> 27:13.000
-Oh.
-[Arthur] Yeah, well,

27:14.040 --> 27:15.200
something to do.

27:17.000 --> 27:18.040
I wanna open a garage.

27:19.160 --> 27:20.720
-Someday.
-Fixing cars, you know?

27:20.880 --> 27:22.880
Sometimes cars attract ambitious men.

27:24.320 --> 27:25.320
Yeah, but...

27:26.760 --> 27:28.800
-I like fixing cars.
-Hmm.

27:31.200 --> 27:32.640
[telephone ringing]

27:33.560 --> 27:34.560
I'll go.

27:34.960 --> 27:35.960
I got it.

27:41.840 --> 27:43.440
Maypole 245.

27:44.480 --> 27:45.480
Arthur,

27:45.800 --> 27:46.960
have you checked your post?

27:48.400 --> 27:50.080
I just got served a black hand.

27:51.680 --> 27:54.040
I just got delivered
a black fucking hand to the house

27:55.200 --> 27:56.480
from Luca Changretta.

27:57.640 --> 27:58.640
Jesus.

28:00.560 --> 28:01.560
Jesus Christ!

28:04.920 --> 28:06.680
Wait a minute, John, which one's Luca?

28:07.480 --> 28:08.640
The old man's only son,

28:09.960 --> 28:12.600
he was gonna get done
for killing a bank clerk in a robbery.

28:13.120 --> 28:15.160
So his old man sent him back to New York.

28:16.400 --> 28:18.720
You know what the black hand
means among the wops, Arthur?

28:20.000 --> 28:21.080
It's mafia shit.

28:22.360 --> 28:24.120
The Sicilian fucking mafia.

28:25.600 --> 28:26.840
Just check your post, Arthur.

28:35.200 --> 28:36.560
Arthur, I was just leaving.

28:36.680 --> 28:37.680
[Arthur] No, you're not.

28:38.800 --> 28:40.960
I need... I need to talk to you.

28:41.440 --> 28:42.920
-Arthur?
-It's all right, Linda.

28:43.560 --> 28:45.320
Stay here. Ada, please?

28:50.120 --> 28:52.360
Linda, you stay here.

29:02.560 --> 29:03.840
Did you say mafia?

29:04.880 --> 29:06.200
Esme, I need to make a call.

29:07.120 --> 29:08.120
No.

29:08.200 --> 29:09.720
I need to make a fucking call. Gimme...

29:09.800 --> 29:10.840
What the fuck is this?

29:11.200 --> 29:13.040
Not until you tell me what the fuck it is.

29:13.120 --> 29:14.600
-Give it here.
-What is it?

29:15.440 --> 29:18.320
It's from Luca Changretta,
Arthur killed his dad.

29:19.480 --> 29:20.480
I remember.

29:21.000 --> 29:22.000
It was Tommy who killed him.

29:22.080 --> 29:24.680
It was fucking...
Arthur pulled the trigger.

29:25.560 --> 29:27.640
All right, it was mercy,
but it was Arthur.

29:28.520 --> 29:30.280
Anyway, it makes no fucking difference.

29:30.840 --> 29:32.080
For the wops, it's family.

29:33.000 --> 29:34.320
The black hand came here,

29:34.560 --> 29:35.880
everybody will have got one,

29:36.600 --> 29:37.720
they're coming for us all.

29:42.960 --> 29:44.680
We made an agreement.

29:45.680 --> 29:47.480
We made a solemn promise,

29:48.880 --> 29:50.120
we're the family now.

29:51.240 --> 29:53.720
[In Romani]
We can look after ourselves.

29:59.920 --> 30:01.760
Here, look at that.

30:03.040 --> 30:05.920
That's from Changretta's son, Luca.

30:06.720 --> 30:09.880
How the fuck he knows where I live, eh?

30:10.520 --> 30:11.880
And why has he waited a year?

30:13.040 --> 30:15.080
I'm gonna see Tommy next,
I'll talk to him.

30:16.640 --> 30:18.160
I've been served a black hand

30:18.880 --> 30:21.560
and she won't even let me keep
a fucking spud gun in the house.

30:21.640 --> 30:22.720
Go to a hotel.

30:23.240 --> 30:24.880
It's Christmas Eve, Ada.

30:28.880 --> 30:31.360
I've got a gun in the glove compartment,
you take that for now.

30:31.680 --> 30:34.720
I'll talk to Tommy and have him call,
just make sure you get to the phone first.

30:34.800 --> 30:36.240
-Yeah.
-Now,

30:36.840 --> 30:38.960
hug me like you came out here
'cause you were emotional.

30:39.640 --> 30:40.640
I am emotional.

30:41.360 --> 30:43.280
I just don't know
what fucking emotion it is.

30:44.920 --> 30:47.360
It'll be okay. I'll talk to Tommy.

30:47.760 --> 30:48.760
You talk to him.

30:55.560 --> 30:57.160
You and me both, brother.

31:04.520 --> 31:05.520
[Arthur] Ada?

31:07.120 --> 31:08.120
You wait there.

31:08.680 --> 31:10.840
You won't leave empty-handed,
here you go, look,

31:11.200 --> 31:13.200
some eggs, you get them
to Polly, all right?

31:14.080 --> 31:16.240
And you, keep your eyes on the road.

31:18.160 --> 31:19.160
Take care.

31:27.360 --> 31:28.600
Who was on the phone, Arthur?

31:29.240 --> 31:31.880
John, wishing me Merry Christmas.

31:36.400 --> 31:37.400
Come inside,

31:38.000 --> 31:39.000
it's getting late.

31:40.880 --> 31:44.320
-[ship horn blowing]
-[indistinct chatter]

32:02.000 --> 32:03.000
Thanks.

32:17.040 --> 32:19.040
[speaking Italian]

32:31.640 --> 32:32.800
Take off the hat.

32:40.480 --> 32:41.960
Are you with those other Italians?

32:43.200 --> 32:44.760
We're Americans,

32:45.520 --> 32:47.320
says it right there on the paper.

32:48.880 --> 32:50.080
USA.

32:53.840 --> 32:55.280
And what's the purpose of your visit?

32:57.560 --> 32:58.560
Pleasure.

33:11.560 --> 33:13.320
Mum? It's me.

33:20.640 --> 33:21.720
Left the door open.

33:21.960 --> 33:23.000
To change the air.

33:23.840 --> 33:25.440
I told you I was busy today,
what do you want?

33:28.000 --> 33:29.240
Why haven't you opened your post?

33:30.640 --> 33:31.640
Tidied up.

33:33.320 --> 33:34.720
Ada's coming today.

33:35.360 --> 33:36.480
She's late.

33:37.720 --> 33:39.080
Tommy asked about you today.

33:42.080 --> 33:43.840
I hope Ada's car hasn't broken down.

33:44.800 --> 33:46.800
Shelby Company Limited
still using Bentleys?

33:47.680 --> 33:48.680
Yeah.

33:49.880 --> 33:52.160
Bentleys are no good in the cold.
You should tell him.

33:53.360 --> 33:54.440
[sighs] I will.

33:56.120 --> 33:57.440
Any other messages for Tommy?

33:57.560 --> 33:58.720
Yeah, fuck off.

34:01.480 --> 34:03.280
He saw that your drainpipe was broken.

34:04.640 --> 34:05.640
He's worried.

34:09.199 --> 34:10.199
Is that it?

34:10.600 --> 34:11.960
Is that all he asked about, drainpipes?

34:13.040 --> 34:15.440
No, he said that I'm to accept
that you have a gift.

34:17.280 --> 34:18.560
That you've always had a gift.

34:20.199 --> 34:21.199
What gift?

34:22.280 --> 34:23.280
Second sight.

34:24.679 --> 34:26.280
Spirits, all that gypsy stuff.

34:26.480 --> 34:27.719
He said that I'm to believe you.

34:27.920 --> 34:30.000
You think I don't hear his voice in yours?

34:30.600 --> 34:32.520
You don't think
I recognize his strategies?

34:34.360 --> 34:36.199
-I'm still a match for him.
-Yes,

34:37.199 --> 34:38.199
you are.

34:39.199 --> 34:40.239
And you still can be.

34:42.280 --> 34:43.480
Me and Lizzie decided

34:44.080 --> 34:46.920
that this new year
we're all to turn a page.

34:49.719 --> 34:51.320
You can't spend
another year like this, Mum.

34:51.400 --> 34:52.400
Mum.

34:58.520 --> 34:59.520
Mum.

35:01.520 --> 35:03.000
Word is like a bullet to me.

35:10.240 --> 35:12.400
See your sister in that chair sometimes.

35:16.360 --> 35:17.360
Look,

35:18.480 --> 35:19.560
me and Lizzie decided,

35:22.800 --> 35:23.800
it's time.

35:27.200 --> 35:28.200
I bought these.

35:30.040 --> 35:31.080
One for you and Ada...

35:32.000 --> 35:33.000
One for you and me.

35:35.400 --> 35:37.120
So Tommy said, keep her off the whiskey?

35:42.200 --> 35:45.840
I'll drink champagne the day my son leaves
the employment of Shelby Company Limited.

35:47.600 --> 35:50.240
You tell him that next time
he mentions fucking drainpipes.

36:07.440 --> 36:10.400
Right, now, this is your job, Charlie.

36:11.880 --> 36:14.080
Wanna give those to Santa,

36:15.080 --> 36:16.080
to Rudolph.

36:16.640 --> 36:17.840
Good boy.

36:18.360 --> 36:20.280
Leave this out for Santa, that's whiskey.

36:21.200 --> 36:24.160
Now, night night, Merry Christmas.

36:26.640 --> 36:28.880
I'll see you tomorrow.
All right? Sleep well.

36:28.960 --> 36:29.960
[Frances] Come on, Charlie.

37:41.440 --> 37:42.440
[knock at door]

37:55.000 --> 37:56.280
Mr. Shelby, it's your sister.

37:56.800 --> 37:58.520
I know. Send her in.

38:06.040 --> 38:09.080
I've had a card, Ada. I'm guessing
Arthur and John have had one as well.

38:09.920 --> 38:12.520
"Hello, Tommy."
"Hello, Ada, welcome home."

38:12.600 --> 38:13.760
"Thanks, it's nice to be back."

38:17.680 --> 38:18.680
I've spoken to Moss.

38:19.200 --> 38:21.760
Moss says that Changretta
is a soldier for the Spinietta family,

38:21.840 --> 38:24.040
which means that he'll have men with him,
professional men.

38:24.120 --> 38:27.080
They usually operate
in units of around ten.

38:27.200 --> 38:29.960
Moss is checking Cunard records
to see if they're already in England.

38:30.600 --> 38:31.600
This one's for you.

38:33.520 --> 38:34.960
What is it, a time machine?

38:35.720 --> 38:38.600
My God, Tommy Shelby, is that regret?

38:39.320 --> 38:40.400
I'll open it tomorrow.

38:41.720 --> 38:42.800
So, boss,

38:43.040 --> 38:46.520
in light of the changed circumstances,
what are your orders?

38:50.200 --> 38:51.840
Changretta knows where we all live.

38:53.120 --> 38:55.920
If we stay out in the open, isolated,
he'll pick us off one by one.

38:57.120 --> 38:59.560
We need to be together in a place
even they won't dare to come.

39:01.600 --> 39:02.720
You mean, back home?

39:04.120 --> 39:07.520
Within a four-mile radius of the Garrison.
Every man is a guard and a soldier for us.

39:07.920 --> 39:09.160
I'm calling a family meeting.

39:09.640 --> 39:11.280
Charlie Strong's yard, Boxing Day.

39:12.120 --> 39:13.120
Finn's already there.

39:13.600 --> 39:15.720
You tell Polly and Michael,
I'll deal with John and Arthur.

39:15.880 --> 39:17.280
And Esme and Linda?

39:19.800 --> 39:21.720
Anyone who wants to live
to see another Christmas

39:21.800 --> 39:24.840
needs to come where it's safe.
These bastards will kill kids as well.

39:25.040 --> 39:26.840
When this business is finished we can...

39:27.480 --> 39:28.800
go our separate ways.

39:31.560 --> 39:34.240
Go and see Polly and explain.
She'll have had a card as well.

39:36.560 --> 39:38.320
Do you think I'm on the list?

39:39.840 --> 39:41.280
We're all on the list, Ada.

39:43.760 --> 39:45.000
I gave my gun to Arthur.

40:03.760 --> 40:04.760
Welcome home.

40:05.360 --> 40:06.360
[scoffs]

40:23.600 --> 40:24.840
Holy shit.

40:25.480 --> 40:27.480
-It's Father Christmas.
-Yeah.

40:28.400 --> 40:29.560
And if you're good

40:30.600 --> 40:31.760
you get what you deserve.

40:32.640 --> 40:33.640
Fucking come here, girl.

40:52.520 --> 40:54.280
[phone ringing]

40:59.200 --> 41:00.800
[phone continues ringing]

41:08.680 --> 41:09.680
Fuck.

41:17.800 --> 41:20.040
Yeah, put me through to Maypole 245.

41:20.600 --> 41:22.080
[phone ringing]

41:30.280 --> 41:31.280
Hello?

41:31.480 --> 41:32.520
Arthur, it's Tommy.

41:33.400 --> 41:34.760
Be quick, they're asleep.

41:35.640 --> 41:38.760
Family meeting, Charlie's Yard,
Boxing Day, midday.

41:39.520 --> 41:42.240
I can't raise John
but I'll send Michael to get him.

41:43.280 --> 41:45.360
If you have to pull a gun on Linda, do it.

41:45.800 --> 41:46.800
Merry Christmas.

41:52.520 --> 41:53.880
Merry Christmas, Tom.

42:03.840 --> 42:04.880
What did you do with them?

42:07.200 --> 42:09.600
My tablets were in the bathroom cabinet.
What did you do with them?

42:11.120 --> 42:12.520
I threw them in the lavatory.

42:14.480 --> 42:17.120
-Tommy's orders?
-No. My own decision.

42:22.600 --> 42:25.520
How am I gonna get through Christmas
without them? They close everything.

42:26.080 --> 42:27.680
How am I gonna get through Christmas
without them?

42:27.760 --> 42:29.680
-I'll help you.
-They don't open anything.

42:29.920 --> 42:31.320
Fucking no apothecary, nothing.

42:32.640 --> 42:34.760
You can move in with me and I'll help you.

42:36.080 --> 42:37.680
How am I gonna get through
fucking Christmas,

42:38.280 --> 42:40.280
without... without anything?

42:40.760 --> 42:43.800
[breathing heavily]

42:45.600 --> 42:47.400
You can move in with me and I'll help you.

42:47.480 --> 42:51.920
Fuck off. Fuck off.
Fuck off, Thomas Shelby. Fuck off.

42:52.000 --> 42:54.200
It's all right, it's me.
Mom, this has got to stop!

42:54.280 --> 42:56.120
-I just want the tablets.
-This has got to stop!

42:56.200 --> 42:58.680
Tommy said to believe in spirits with you
but I can't.

42:58.760 --> 42:59.760
Hello, Polly.

43:00.080 --> 43:01.080
Hello, Michael.

43:02.120 --> 43:03.440
Merry Christmas.

43:04.080 --> 43:05.480
Door was wide open.

43:06.120 --> 43:07.120
Fuck.

43:08.520 --> 43:11.600
I spent the whole day tidying up,
I wanted it to be nice.

43:12.200 --> 43:13.640
I wanted it to look nice.

43:13.720 --> 43:15.320
All right, Pol, it's only me.

43:16.040 --> 43:18.360
It's okay. It's okay, we can sit.

43:18.640 --> 43:22.520
Sit and talk, we'll put things
back together. It's okay.

43:23.760 --> 43:25.960
-I'll leave you two to it.
-No, you stay.

43:28.240 --> 43:29.240
Now listen,

43:29.360 --> 43:30.560
something's happened.

43:31.000 --> 43:32.080
Things have changed.

43:33.080 --> 43:35.560
Today, everyone in the family

43:36.400 --> 43:37.640
received one of these.

43:49.040 --> 43:50.040
What does it mean?

43:50.440 --> 43:51.880
[Ada] Tommy's called a family meeting.

43:52.840 --> 43:54.040
He wants you both to come.

44:02.200 --> 44:03.240
[knock at door]

44:05.280 --> 44:06.280
Come.

44:13.720 --> 44:15.480
I'm really sorry to bother you again, sir,

44:16.360 --> 44:18.880
but Chef insists on knowing
what time the guests will arrive.

44:21.000 --> 44:22.880
Frances, for the last time,

44:23.880 --> 44:25.120
it's Johnny Dogs,

44:25.640 --> 44:26.640
they're gypsies,

44:26.960 --> 44:28.240
they're camped down by the river,

44:28.400 --> 44:29.680
when they're ready they'll walk up.

44:30.200 --> 44:31.200
All right?

44:31.880 --> 44:33.360
He says it's about preparation, sir.

44:33.440 --> 44:34.440
What is?

44:34.720 --> 44:36.000
He's asked specifically,

44:36.880 --> 44:39.200
will they arrive
before the King's speech or after?

44:44.480 --> 44:45.760
You said he was new, this chef.

44:48.480 --> 44:50.880
-When did he join us?
-October.

44:55.360 --> 44:56.360
October.

44:58.640 --> 44:59.640
And he's foreign?

45:00.080 --> 45:01.960
-He's Italian, sir.
-Oh.

45:04.560 --> 45:06.440
He's the best chef
we've ever had in the house.

45:07.720 --> 45:10.040
No shouting or swearing or blaspheming.

45:10.440 --> 45:12.480
-Do we have his references?
-Yes.

45:15.760 --> 45:17.800
The only problem has been his assistant.

45:18.400 --> 45:19.400
What assistant?

45:19.480 --> 45:21.000
He brought an assistant with him,

45:21.440 --> 45:22.680
he calls him his sous chef.

45:27.520 --> 45:29.360
Are they still working, Frances?

45:29.520 --> 45:31.120
They'll be there till midnight, sir.

45:36.800 --> 45:38.720
All right, thank you.
Goodnight, you can go to bed.

45:40.280 --> 45:41.520
Merry Christmas, sir.

45:43.880 --> 45:45.200
And I thought about your offer,

45:47.400 --> 45:49.200
I'd be happy to sit at your table.

45:51.160 --> 45:52.160
All right, thank you.

46:22.240 --> 46:23.240
Mr. Shelby.

46:31.960 --> 46:32.960
What's your name?

46:33.120 --> 46:34.800
-Max, Mr. Shelby.
-Max.

46:38.280 --> 46:39.520
It's all right, don't get up.

46:40.400 --> 46:41.400
Oh.

46:42.160 --> 46:43.280
Sorry, sorry, sir.

46:46.840 --> 46:48.360
You're new. I'm Mr. Shelby.

46:48.960 --> 46:49.960
Hello, sir.

46:51.480 --> 46:53.520
I haven't taken time to introduce myself.

46:55.040 --> 46:56.040
Antonio.

47:00.320 --> 47:01.840
What have you done that's so wrong, eh?

47:03.600 --> 47:04.600
Excuse me?

47:05.000 --> 47:06.000
Sous chef,

47:06.640 --> 47:07.640
peeling potatoes?

47:10.000 --> 47:12.160
It's an emergency, late notice.

47:12.920 --> 47:15.560
Oh, late notice.

47:16.680 --> 47:17.680
All right.

47:18.760 --> 47:19.760
All right, carry on.

47:28.760 --> 47:29.760
Antonio,

47:31.320 --> 47:32.320
here £10...

47:34.880 --> 47:35.920
for the late notice.

48:14.920 --> 48:16.520
You wanted to know
if my guests would arrive

48:16.600 --> 48:18.320
before or after the King's speech.

48:22.440 --> 48:23.760
-Eh?
-Yeah.

48:26.680 --> 48:27.680
It'll be after.

48:37.280 --> 48:38.280
How are you?

48:39.280 --> 48:41.840
Just... worried about tomorrow.

48:44.280 --> 48:45.880
Yeah, I'm worried about Antonio.

48:51.760 --> 48:55.040
You've been here two months
and we've not met before, it's my fault.

48:55.800 --> 48:56.800
I've been busy.

48:58.600 --> 48:59.600
Thomas Shelby.

49:03.200 --> 49:04.200
My hand has blood.

49:04.440 --> 49:05.560
Oh, mine too.

49:08.960 --> 49:12.760
Hey, how much do you pay Antonio?

49:15.480 --> 49:16.480
I forget.

49:17.440 --> 49:18.440
Must be a lot.

49:19.560 --> 49:21.120
I just gave him £10,

49:21.840 --> 49:23.400
didn't mean a fucking thing to him.

49:27.840 --> 49:29.280
Maybe it isn't you that pays him.

49:42.600 --> 49:43.920
I've been reading up on you

49:44.240 --> 49:46.520
Bertorelli, Claridge's.

49:47.520 --> 49:50.640
You used to work in a place
called San Marcos...

49:52.080 --> 49:53.080
on...

49:54.600 --> 49:55.600
on Fleet Street.

49:58.600 --> 50:00.560
I used to know the man
that owns San Marcos,

50:02.000 --> 50:03.240
a man called Darby Sabini?

50:05.440 --> 50:06.920
-I never met him.
-No.

50:08.600 --> 50:10.760
Maybe your, um, assistant...

50:11.680 --> 50:13.160
Antonio, maybe he's met him.

50:16.200 --> 50:17.200
Is that what he is?

50:18.240 --> 50:19.280
Antonio was sent from New York?

50:19.360 --> 50:20.880
I don't know, please.

50:21.000 --> 50:22.640
Darby Sabini facilitated.

50:22.800 --> 50:25.040
He passed him onto you,
told you to bring him into my house,

50:25.560 --> 50:27.040
threatened to kill you
if you didn't do it.

50:29.080 --> 50:31.160
Do you want me to dress you
like you dressed that fucking stag?

50:31.280 --> 50:32.680
Please, don't...

50:35.720 --> 50:37.240
-You know about me?
-Mmm-hmm.

50:37.680 --> 50:38.680
All right.

50:39.600 --> 50:40.880
-You know what I do?
-Mmm-hmm.

50:43.520 --> 50:44.880
You wanted to know
when my guests would arrive

50:44.960 --> 50:46.480
'cause Antonio needed me alone.

50:47.280 --> 50:50.320
He's an assassin,
the plan is to kill me tomorrow.

50:52.920 --> 50:54.880
I don't know.

50:55.600 --> 50:57.560
They just said bring him here.

51:02.680 --> 51:03.800
Well, bring him here.

51:09.320 --> 51:10.320
Antonio...

51:11.920 --> 51:14.560
[speaking Italian]

51:44.360 --> 51:45.360
Oh.

51:45.880 --> 51:47.120
[speaking Italian]

52:05.840 --> 52:07.080
You're a black hand!

52:08.680 --> 52:09.840
You're a black hand!

52:10.480 --> 52:11.560
How many came from New York?

52:11.960 --> 52:14.440
Eh, how many fucking came from New York?

52:14.640 --> 52:15.800
[speaking Italian]

52:17.600 --> 52:21.000
What did he say? Is that a curse
or a number, what did he fucking say?

52:21.440 --> 52:22.680
What did he fucking say?

52:22.760 --> 52:24.680
-He said fuck you.
-Yeah?

52:25.800 --> 52:26.800
[screams]

52:36.520 --> 52:39.080
Black hand means kill or be killed.

52:40.800 --> 52:41.960
You go back to London,

52:42.880 --> 52:44.200
you tell Darby Sabini

52:44.960 --> 52:46.800
he picked the wrong side in this war.

52:48.360 --> 52:49.800
Once we've dealt with the Americans,

52:50.360 --> 52:51.360
we're coming for him.

52:51.760 --> 52:53.240
Go on, go.

52:54.040 --> 52:55.280
Go. Oi,

52:56.000 --> 52:58.920
you tell anyone else,
I'll come and find you.

53:18.560 --> 53:19.680
Harrow, 335.

53:21.360 --> 53:22.680
The Hare and the Hounds pub.

53:29.160 --> 53:31.480
Robert, yes, it's Mr. Shelby.

53:33.320 --> 53:34.680
Merry Christmas to you too.

53:35.720 --> 53:38.960
Robert, is there a gypsy in the public bar
playing the fiddle for shillings?

53:39.880 --> 53:40.880
Yes,

53:41.640 --> 53:42.640
can you, uh,

53:43.320 --> 53:44.800
can you tell him I need to speak to him?

53:45.640 --> 53:46.640
Thank you.

53:59.000 --> 54:00.400
Oh, fuck, Tom.

54:01.360 --> 54:03.120
I thought your sporting days were over.

54:03.280 --> 54:04.440
Yeah, so did I,

54:04.920 --> 54:06.320
they keep coming back at us.

54:08.240 --> 54:11.560
There's a black stallion in the stables,
he's invisible at night, use him.

54:12.560 --> 54:14.640
Take the body across the river
to the rough ground.

54:16.000 --> 54:19.000
-Burn him?
-No. This one's a message.

54:20.360 --> 54:21.880
Will there still be geese for dinner?

54:22.480 --> 54:24.280
Only if you can steal it on the way.

54:24.720 --> 54:25.720
On the way where?

54:26.840 --> 54:28.560
We're going back, Johnny.

54:31.000 --> 54:32.000
Back to Small Heath.

54:32.680 --> 54:34.040
Back where you belong.

54:35.040 --> 54:37.880
[In Romani]
You're the wild Gypsy boy, Tommy, forever.

54:38.080 --> 54:40.480
[Tommy, in English] Merry Christmas,
you can keep the stallion.

54:41.000 --> 54:42.600
Christ the fucking night.

54:57.960 --> 54:59.640
[Tommy] Michael, they're coming today.

55:00.040 --> 55:02.040
No, Michael, shut up and listen.

55:02.640 --> 55:06.080
Gotta get everyone out,
get Polly and Ada to Charlie's Yard.

55:06.200 --> 55:07.880
I've told Arthur but I can't reach John.

55:08.000 --> 55:11.120
When you've dropped Polly and Ada,
go to John's place and get him out.

55:11.360 --> 55:12.360
All right?

55:14.880 --> 55:17.760
-Is it Christmas?
-Not just yet. But let's go, eh?

55:18.640 --> 55:19.640
Mummy.

55:29.320 --> 55:30.320
Come on!

55:31.360 --> 55:32.360
Move.

55:46.680 --> 55:47.680
Hello?

55:51.440 --> 55:52.760
[gun cocking]

55:54.720 --> 55:55.840
Oh, fuck, it's you.

55:56.800 --> 55:58.440
Got nothing better to do
on Christmas morning?

55:58.840 --> 56:01.200
Tommy wants everybody
at Charlie's Yard now, come on.

56:02.440 --> 56:03.640
Get in! Get in!

56:03.840 --> 56:05.840
What's gonna happen, man,
it's fucking Christmas.

56:06.360 --> 56:08.360
Look, John, we don't have time for this,

56:08.640 --> 56:11.280
-all right? Just come to the meeting.
-Just come in the house, have some food.

56:13.080 --> 56:14.440
-Hey.
-Tell Tommy Shelby

56:14.520 --> 56:15.520
we can look after ourselves.

56:15.600 --> 56:17.000
Tommy says that
they could come for us today.

56:17.080 --> 56:19.080
Tommy says, Tommy says.
Are you his fucking parrot?

56:19.160 --> 56:20.560
Look, it's the mafia, all right?

56:21.160 --> 56:23.240
This is the New York mafia
we're talking about.

56:23.320 --> 56:25.200
And we're the Peaky fucking Blinders.

56:25.280 --> 56:26.280
No, we're not, John.

56:27.000 --> 56:29.400
We're not the Peaky fucking Blinders
unless we're together.

56:30.160 --> 56:31.720
You were together in the gallows

56:31.920 --> 56:33.360
with one man missing.

56:34.680 --> 56:35.680
John.

56:36.280 --> 56:38.800
John, come to the meeting.
All right? Think about the kids.

56:39.480 --> 56:41.800
Come to the meeting
and if you want to leave, then fine.

56:42.680 --> 56:44.560
No. It's Christmas day,

56:45.240 --> 56:47.160
we're the family now,
we're staying at home.

56:50.600 --> 56:52.080
-Get in the fucking house!
-Esme.

56:54.560 --> 56:55.560
John!

57:34.240 --> 57:36.840
♪ On a gathering storm comes ♪

57:36.920 --> 57:38.320
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

57:38.400 --> 57:40.360
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

57:40.440 --> 57:42.840
♪ A red right hand ♪
